    dict(key='08-act-3', kind='console', title='Act Three — Insertion and deletion at both ends and in the middle',
         body='THREE. Insertion and deletion at both ends and in the middle.\n  insertAtBeginning("airport"): 3 pointer changes\n  insertAtEnd("river"): 0 steps, 3 pointer changes\n  insertAtPosition(3, "garden"): 2 steps, 4 pointer changes\n  deleteAtEnd() removed "river": 0 steps, 2 pointer changes, through tail\n  deleteByKey("cake"): 3 comparisons, 2 pointer changes, no prev pointer to keep\n  head -> airport <-> beach <-> garden <-> dog <-> forest <-> mountain <- tail',
         narration='Now the textbook operations. [[slnc 400]] Inserting at the beginning or at the end sets three pointers, with no walking. [[slnc 400]] Inserting at position three walks two steps, then sets four pointers. [[slnc 500]] Deleting at the end goes straight through the tail. [[slnc 300]] A singly linked list would have to walk the whole list. [[slnc 500]] And deleting the cake points its two neighbours at each other.'),
